  "body": "## Why\n\nThe maintainer wrote (2026-11-17): \"WCS54, X flipped - posting and generating are refused until the flip is cleared..  the ability to flip axis from a positive to negative is fundamental and should not be blocked.. posting and generation should take it into consideration rather..\"\n\n## What changed\n\n- Generation, verification and the stock simulation no longer refuse a flipped setup. They stay in the setup frame, so the cut does not change.\n- The job writes `PARAM WcsFlip` on each section of a flipped setup. A new post pass (`crates/post/src/post/wcs_flip.rs`) runs before `wcs_rotate` and `invert`. It mirrors the flipped axis about the work origin through `invert::translate_rules`.\n- One flipped axis swaps G2/G3 and G41/G42. Two flipped axes (X and Y) keep them. Helix, canned cycles and probing (with `probeAxisInversion`) are carried.\n- The flip composes with a machine-inverted axis.\n- The travel check, the setup sheet and the viewport work envelope read the posted sign.\n- `fanuc.cps` and `haas.cps` state `axisInversion = true` and name the flipped axes in the program header.\n- The MCP flip tool and `get_job` report the refusal only for the cases that still refuse.\n\n## Cases\n\nCarried: Flip X, Flip Y, and Flip X+Y on 3-axis mill sections, with Fanuc and Haas.\n\nRefused by name, with the flip as the cause:\n\n- a flipped Z (follow-up #2474)\n- a script without `axisInversion = true` (follow-up #2475)\n- a flip together with a WCS rotation (follow-up #2476)\n- turning, threading, live tool, ABC/tilt, EDM, wire and plasma sections\n- a section that uses a modal origin or start across a change of flip\n- a `WcsFlip` value that the pass cannot read\n\nThe decision file `docs/decisions/1649-wcs-flip-carry.md` has the case table and the reasons.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/post/tests/wcs_flip.rs` (13 tests), for example `a_flipped_wcs_cuts_the_cam_path`, `one_flipped_axis_reverses_arcs_and_the_compensation_side_and_two_do_not`, `a_flipped_axis_on_an_inverted_machine_axis_posts_the_standard_signs`, `a_flipped_z_refuses_by_name`, `a_flipped_and_rotated_section_refuses_by_name`, `a_section_that_leans_on_a_modal_origin_across_a_flip_change_refuses`\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_flip_post.rs` (8 tests), for example `a_flipped_x_or_y_posts_the_mirrored_program_and_clearing_it_posts_as_before`, `generation_runs_in_a_flipped_setup_and_the_toolpath_does_not_change`, `the_travel_check_reads_the_posted_sign_of_a_flipped_axis`, `the_work_envelope_mirrors_about_the_origin_on_a_flipped_axis`\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_flip.rs` (7 tests), with `the_mcp_tool_sets_the_flags_and_get_job_shows_them`\n- `crates/ui` `wcs_flip_tests`\n\n## Gate\n\nQuick gate (`gate-logs/quick-20261118-074008`): 858 steps, 857 ok. The one red step is clippy on `crates/app/src/operation/heights.rs:128` (`.map(&resolve)`). That lint is on main before this branch and is tracked by #2479. This branch does not touch that file. Clippy of the touched crates with that one lint allowed is clean. `git merge-tree` with `origin/main` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The other post scripts (they refuse until #2475 verifies them).\n- A real controller.\n- Lathe and multi-axis programs (they refuse by name).\n\n## Labels and notes\n\nEffort: max. The issue did not escalate.\n\nProcess change: yes (one row in the `camcraft-mcp` skill).\n\nChangelog: A setup's Flip X / Flip Y no longer refuses generation and the post: Fanuc and Haas programs mirror the flipped axis, with the arc direction and compensation side kept correct. A flipped Z and the other post scripts still refuse by name.\n\nFixes #1649\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
